[3] Status-first proof target
  The theorem should not first ask for route purity.  It should prove:
    in each automatic/residue fiber, coarse ET+Henselian-unit data cannot
    identify an AP/GW boundary equality atom with a strict-open packet.
  Once that is proved, the remaining route-mixed fibers are harmless for
  LRC14 itself and can be discharged by certificate teeth:
    q<=13 direct witness; AP/GW zero-bar equality; strict safe stick or
    Fejer/Haar certificate; unit-petal; K33/F7/THM-572 state lift;
    covering-moment; magnitude-cocycle family formula.

